{"_id":"0a5eabe777fb9a35","name":"Augmenter","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/amplifier.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.amplifier.augmenter","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.amplifier","profession":"Amplifier","summary":"A self-enhancing caster who adapts by augmenting core abilities with magic.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Varies","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Wisdom"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Strength"],"bonusSkill":"Resist Damage","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Individual"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Enhanced Augmentation","type":"Trait","text":"When casting an augmentation spell on yourself, choose Potency, Duration, or Duplication. Only one enhanced augmentation can be active at a time."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/amplifier.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"12","description":"Augmenters split off from early Berserkers. Instead of using their rage to enhance their abilities they learned to use magic. This shift in philosophy made them much more adaptable to situations by augmenting their core abilities.\n\nAugmenters shift their focus from melee attacks to ranged assaults using augmentation magic. New Augmenters start by learning to resist damage. The path to becoming experienced is arduous for the Augmenter. An experienced Augmenter is a nightmare in the living flesh. The Galactic Federation sends these individuals as one or two person teams to deal with discrete issues. Before knowing what has happened, encampments lay in ruin with the best guess that it was done by someone that was unable to handle their cyberware."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2000000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Amplifiers enhance themselves and allies while inhibiting enemies with specialized intrinsic magic.","disciplineSummary":"A self-enhancing caster who adapts by augmenting core abilities with magic.","abilities":[{"name":"Enhanced Augmentation","type":"Trait","text":"When casting an augmentation spell on yourself, choose Potency, Duration, or Duplication. Only one enhanced augmentation can be active at a time."}],"profession":"Amplifier","discipline":"Augmenter"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"0e0f21b38e574687","name":"Walker Operator","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.vehicle-pilot.walker-operator","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.vehicle-pilot","profession":"Vehicle Pilot","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":4800000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Vehicle Pilot","discipline":"Walker Operator","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"13563bbdb926c1ff","name":"Warrior","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/berserker.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.berserker.warrior","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.berserker","profession":"Berserker","summary":"A rage-based martial combatant that escalates close-quarters fights with deadly force and aggression.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Great Axe","primaryAttributes":["Strength","Reaction"],"bonusAttributes":["Agility","Strength"],"bonusSkill":"Rage","persona":["+5 Ruthless","+5 Criminal"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Last Word","type":"Reaction","text":"Make a decisive strike when a foe tries to leave your reach. The strike deals one higher damage threshold, triples critical damage, and increases your damage by 1d8 for the next round. Once per Field Recovery."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/berserker.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"3","description":"Born from oppression, the systems that used to control the Warrior instead forged them into an individual that was far more dangerous. Warriors transform their raw pain, fury, and defiance into an unwavering resolve. Every scar is a reminder to the Warrior of what was taken, each battle a chance to emerge stronger. Warriors are often referred to as the modern-day barbarian of legends.\n\nThe Warrior is a force that grows stronger with every strike feeding their fury. Each successful attack, their momentum grows pushing the limit of their body and mind allowing execution of devastating techniques. Once a warrior commits to combat, few can halt their relentless force until victory is claimed or their target concedes."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Berserkers harness innate bodily energy and push beyond normal mortal limits. They excel in close quarters and deliver powerful strikes.","disciplineSummary":"A rage-based martial combatant that escalates close-quarters fights with deadly force and aggression.","abilities":[{"name":"Last Word","type":"Reaction","text":"Make a decisive strike when a foe tries to leave your reach. The strike deals one higher damage threshold, triples critical damage, and increases your damage by 1d8 for the next round. Once per Field Recovery."}],"profession":"Berserker","discipline":"Warrior"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"164b46b0d3ae7da7","name":"Thaumaturge","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.magus.thaumaturge","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.magus","profession":"Magus","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":3500000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Magus","discipline":"Thaumaturge","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"18a554addfb81412","name":"Combat Medic","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-2.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.field-technician.combat-medic","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.field-technician","profession":"Field Technician","summary":"A battlefield healer who keeps allies fighting with emergency stims and medical equipment.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Light Firearms","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusSkill":"Medicine","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Lawful"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Trained Medic","type":"Trait","text":"See PDF page reference."},{"name":"Emergency Stim","type":"Reaction","text":"See PDF page reference."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-2.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"9","description":"Combat Medics are deployed with the Assault Corps of the military for the Galactic Federation. Most of the time Stormtroopers are brought to the on site medical facility where combat medics treat wounds that are gained in battles. Every so often when moving the forward base, Combat Medics are required to operate in the field with their brethren. When their brethren are attacked and wounded, quick thinking the Combat Medic administers stims giving their allies a chance to keep fighting and secure the area.\n\nAfter their tour of duty, Combat Medics usually transition to the private sector medical industry. If they are unable to secure employment, venturing into the gray markets is the next choice of employment for the Combat Medic."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1400000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Field Technicians solve problems with chemistry, companions, explosives, and emergency medical work.","disciplineSummary":"A battlefield healer who keeps allies fighting with emergency stims and medical equipment.","abilities":[{"name":"Trained Medic","type":"Trait","text":"Your time treating patients has given you real world experience. Administering medicine and treating wounds is something you can do quickly. You gain +3 to Medicine checks. You gain an additional hit point of healing for each level of Medicine that you take."},{"name":"Emergency Stim","type":"Reaction","text":"Administer urgent aid when an ally is attacked or wounded, giving them a chance to keep fighting."}],"profession":"Field Technician","discipline":"Combat Medic"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"19c9f04078b648ed","name":"Steel Adept","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/elemental-adept-3.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.elemental-adept.steel-adept","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.elemental-adept","profession":"Elemental Adept","summary":"A metalmancer who bends steel and metal into magical offense and defense.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Metal Magic","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusSkill":"Metal Pinions","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Lawful"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Metal Affinity","type":"Trait","text":"Metal spells gain +5 to attack rolls, +1 more every 10 levels, and +1d8 damage at level 5 and every 5 levels thereafter."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/elemental-adept-3.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"18","description":"Metalmancy was once believed to have been an impossible task. Legends say that a blind Geo Adept who was so aligned with the fabric of reality learned to bend and wield the magic of metal at the age of 16. The art of metalmancy being passed down in her family for generations. Once the Great Houses of Kadion became aware of metalmancy, it was declared as blasphemy, a perversion of geomancy. Anyone who dared to use metalmancy was to be sentenced to death.\n\nThe Four Great Houses of Kadion united against this perversion of geomancy hunting down anyone suspected of using metalmancy. 100 years of genocide left the remaining Steel Adepts few in number. As a last attempt, they left the planet using their forbidden art.\n\nMetalmancy and Steel Adepts have since then thrived on the planet of Azuno. With geomancy and metalmancy at the tips of their fingers, entire cities of Steel were erected covering the entire planet over the course of a few centuries. The people of Azuno consider their way of life safe given their technological advances that were achieved over a short period of time."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":3200000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Elemental Adepts train in schools of elemental magic to alter reality through water, earth, fire, air, steel, or all elements.","disciplineSummary":"A metalmancer who bends steel and metal into magical offense and defense.","abilities":[{"name":"Metal Affinity","type":"Trait","text":"Metal spells gain +5 to attack rolls, +1 more every 10 levels, and +1d8 damage at level 5 and every 5 levels thereafter."}],"profession":"Elemental Adept","discipline":"Steel Adept"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"1e6210148c9466c1","name":"Shocktrooper","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/marksman-2.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.marksman.shocktrooper","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.marksman","profession":"Marksman","summary":"A heavy-weapons specialist suited to explosive encounters, suppressive fire, and battlefield hardware.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Heavy Firearms","primaryAttributes":["Strength","Dexterity"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Strength"],"bonusSkill":"Heavy Firearms","persona":["+10 Collectivist"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Braced Firing","type":"Trait","text":"If you have not moved this round, add +3 to attack rolls."},{"name":"This is My Weapon Now!","type":"Action >>","text":"Take control of or repurpose a stationary weapon or drone emplacement against your enemies."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/marksman-2.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"11","description":"Shocktroopers are part of the Galactic Federation's Military. Tours of duty may have included planetary invasion or riot control. The foils of destruction lead them to be called to an explosive combat encounter turning the tide of a battle at a moment's notice. Once in combat they lay down suppressive fire and dismount stationary drones that enemies have laid down. Upon picking up the drone, you can hear the cackling laugh as they turn the once stationary weapon on their enemies. Once a term has completed Shocktroopers often sign up for corporate conflicts."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1800000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Marksmen leave their mark with projectile weapons and often specialize in a favored style of firearm or bow.","disciplineSummary":"A heavy-weapons specialist suited to explosive encounters, suppressive fire, and battlefield hardware.","abilities":[{"name":"Braced Firing","type":"Trait","text":"If you have not moved this round, add +3 to attack rolls."},{"name":"This is My Weapon Now!","type":"Action >>","text":"Take control of or repurpose a stationary weapon or drone emplacement against your enemies."}],"profession":"Marksman","discipline":"Shocktrooper"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"260cc362f9be8bbb","name":"Samurai","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/duelist.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.duelist.samurai","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.duelist","profession":"Duelist","summary":"A long-blade specialist trained to disable shields and end fights with precise strikes.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Long Blades","primaryAttributes":["Dexterity","Strength"],"bonusAttributes":["Strength","Reaction"],"bonusSkill":"Long Blades","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Collectivist"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Disabling Holshi Shatter","type":"Action >>","text":"With a short blade, strike a Holtzman shield. Outcomes range from no effect to bypassing and disabling the shield for 1d4 or 2d4 turns. Three uses per long rest."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/duelist.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"7","description":"Samurai is a term that has been passed down from feudal Japan on Terra Prime, and has taken on new meaning throughout the centuries. Their training leads them to only strike when absolutely necessary, often preferring surrender to taking their opponent's life.\n\nSamurai gain their proficiency through years of training and patience. Samurai are specialists of long blades and experts with short blades, being able to deal exacting strikes and excel in slashing and piercing damage. With precise strikes they can disable a Holtzman shield in a single blow. This trained specialist is paramount when dealing with advanced shields."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1000000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Duelists are blade masters, often hired for clean work by megacorps and fixers.","disciplineSummary":"A long-blade specialist trained to disable shields and end fights with precise strikes.","abilities":[{"name":"Disabling Holshi Shatter","type":"Action >>","text":"With a short blade, strike a Holtzman shield. Outcomes range from no effect to bypassing and disabling the shield for 1d4 or 2d4 turns. Three uses per long rest."}],"profession":"Duelist","discipline":"Samurai"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
