{"_id":"a38dbbf220c73cd5","name":"Monk","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/martial-artist.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.martial-artist.monk","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.martial-artist","profession":"Martial Artist","summary":"A martial combatant practicing fast, low-powered unarmed strikes, with or without hand weapons.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Unarmed Strikes","primaryAttributes":["Dexterity","Agility"],"bonusAttributes":["Agility","Intelligence"],"bonusSkill":"Endurance","persona":["+5 Collectivist","+5 Empathetic"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Inner Calm","type":"Ability","text":"Remove emotional conditions as if critically successful and heal 1d8 + Wisdom HP. Twice per Field Recovery."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/martial-artist.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"5","description":"The traditions of the Monk have been passed down for generations. Upon taking the oath of their tradition these individuals forgo material needs in priority of finding inner peace and have sworn to only act in defense of others or to restore stability and balance across reality. Monks are generally pacifistic preferring to prevent unnecessary bloodshed whenever possible. Monks and Druids coexist in Monasteries throughout the galaxy. These two groups rely on each other for their communities instead of purchasing corporate products when necessary.\n\nThe Monk has honed their inner strength focusing on lightning fast strikes moving from target to target in split seconds. With additional training they are able to harness magic to augment their strikes. Monks aim to subdue or incapacitate before taking a life."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":500000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Martial Artists refine body, discipline, and precision through combat traditions passed down across generations.","disciplineSummary":"A martial combatant practicing fast, low-powered unarmed strikes, with or without hand weapons.","abilities":[{"name":"Inner Calm","type":"Ability","text":"Remove emotional conditions as if critically successful and heal 1d8 + Wisdom HP. Twice per Field Recovery."}],"profession":"Martial Artist","discipline":"Monk"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"a5c79ab487fddcb9","name":"Multipedal","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.drone-operator.multipedal","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.drone-operator","profession":"Drone Operator","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":5400000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Drone Operator","discipline":"Multipedal","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"a95797380f0fe914","name":"Assassin","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/duelist.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.duelist.assassin","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.duelist","profession":"Duelist","summary":"A melee combatant who exploits weak targets and deals heavy damage to badly injured enemies.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Short Blades","primaryAttributes":["Dexterity","Reaction"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Reaction"],"bonusSkill":"Disarm","persona":["+5 Individual","+5 Ruthless"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Assassinate","type":"Action >>","text":"With a short blade, strike a badly injured target with no active armor, shields, or barrier. Outcomes scale from contested state to triple critical damage. Three uses per long rest."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/duelist.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"7","description":"Assassins are lone wolves operating in the shadows. When a fixer gives the order for a cleaning crew the Assassin is the first one to show up.\n\nAssassins stalk their target waiting for the most opportune time to strike. Moving through the shadows, silently they sneak upon their prey, often cornered in an alley way away from prying eyes. It is here they deliver a single strike exacting death in a singular moment. It is here the Assassin completes their contract for their fixer, just another job done for credits."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":900000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Duelists are blade masters, often hired for clean work by megacorps and fixers.","disciplineSummary":"A melee combatant who exploits weak targets and deals heavy damage to badly injured enemies.","abilities":[{"name":"Assassinate","type":"Action >>","text":"With a short blade, strike a badly injured target with no active armor, shields, or barrier. Outcomes scale from contested state to triple critical damage. Three uses per long rest."}],"profession":"Duelist","discipline":"Assassin"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"aae26af72e04c3a9","name":"Runner","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/gymnast.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.gymnast.runner","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.gymnast","profession":"Gymnast","summary":"An agile courier and escape specialist who excels at covering distance and staying ahead of pursuit.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Unarmed","primaryAttributes":["Agility","Reaction"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Perception"],"bonusSkill":"Disarm","persona":["+5 Individual","+5 Criminal"],"tags":["Mobility","Utility"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trained Runner","type":"Trait","text":"Gain 4m bonus movement every turn."},{"name":"Improved Awareness","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +2 Perception."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/gymnast.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"4","description":"Runners are the backbone of any settlement, traversing information and not so legal packages for clients. Runs require Runners to move fast and quietly. City Runners are masters of parkour using the urban jungle to their advantage. In the lesser developed regions Runners rely on the environment of their landscape to stay hidden. If there are any disruptions the runner must flee as quickly as they possibly can. While not trained in specific weaponry Runners can disarm their opponents as they make their hasty escape."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":300000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Gymnasts are flexible, dexterous, and agile specialists who move through cities, wilds, and difficult spaces with finesse.","disciplineSummary":"An agile courier and escape specialist who excels at covering distance and staying ahead of pursuit.","abilities":[{"name":"Trained Runner","type":"Trait","text":"Gain 4m bonus movement every turn."},{"name":"Improved Awareness","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +2 Perception."}],"profession":"Gymnast","discipline":"Runner"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"ab27d9ab58f161e8","name":"Cultivator","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/druid.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.druid.cultivator","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.druid","profession":"Druid","summary":"An arbormancy caster who uses flora to control movement, cause conditions, and defend enclaves.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Staff","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Wisdom"],"bonusAttributes":["Agility","Intelligence"],"bonusSkill":"Reading of Roots","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Collectivist"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Resplendent Flora","type":"Ability","text":"When flora is available, gain +10 to attack rolls for floral abilities and spells, plus 1d6 floral damage for every five character levels. Once per long rest."},{"name":"Green Thumb","type":"Trait","text":"When casting a spell with the floral trait, gain +1 to the attack roll for every five character levels."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/druid.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"15","description":"Druids that are Cultivators generally stay within the established enclave. Their abilities are used to provide for the enclave nourishment and defense from intruders if it is ever needed. On the rare occasion that a Cultivator does leave the enclave, it is usually due to being exiled. Druids do not tolerate unnecessary violence of their craft unless absolutely necessary. Cultivators that leave their enclave are generally labeled as ecological terrorists as they swarm areas with vines, plants, and other flora."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2600000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Druids commune with nature and stabilize Aether disrupted by corporations and reckless magic users.","disciplineSummary":"An arbormancy caster who uses flora to control movement, cause conditions, and defend enclaves.","abilities":[{"name":"Resplendent Flora","type":"Ability","text":"When flora is available, gain +10 to attack rolls for floral abilities and spells, plus 1d6 floral damage for every five character levels. Once per long rest."},{"name":"Green Thumb","type":"Trait","text":"When casting a spell with the floral trait, gain +1 to the attack roll for every five character levels."}],"profession":"Druid","discipline":"Cultivator"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"b782b9c19af29f4c","name":"Aqueous Adept","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/elemental-adept.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.elemental-adept.aqueous-adept","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.elemental-adept","profession":"Elemental Adept","summary":"A hydromancer who changes the flow and shape of water-based liquids.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Hydro Magic","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Dexterity"],"bonusAttributes":["Agility","Intelligence"],"bonusSkill":"Reading of Water","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Collectivist"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Hydro Affinity","type":"Trait","text":"Hydro spells gain +5 to attack rolls, +1 more every 10 levels, and +1d8 damage at level 5 and every 5 levels thereafter."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/elemental-adept.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"16","description":"Aqueous Adepts originated from the water planet Renviea. The need to prevent the ever increasing ocean levels and river levels found its inhabitants at risk of extinction. When all hope seemed lost, the forgotten hero of Renviea stood on the Spire Coast. The history books lie blank for what happened that day other than it being the turning moment for the people of Renviea. The day lives in legend as the moment that ensured survivals into what is known as the Thousand Year War.\n\nThe people of Renviea have since then learned to connect with their homeworld, guided by the ebbs and flows of the fervent hydro energy connections within the celestial body. As of this day they live in a harmonic relationship with the planet."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2800000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Elemental Adepts train in schools of elemental magic to alter reality through water, earth, fire, air, steel, or all elements.","disciplineSummary":"A hydromancer who changes the flow and shape of water-based liquids.","abilities":[{"name":"Hydro Affinity","type":"Trait","text":"Hydro spells gain +5 to attack rolls, +1 more every 10 levels, and +1d8 damage at level 5 and every 5 levels thereafter."}],"profession":"Elemental Adept","discipline":"Aqueous Adept"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"bc0db97c51471430","name":"Illusionist","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/conjurer.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.conjurer.illusionist","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.conjurer","profession":"Conjurer","summary":"A caster who creates illusions and phantasms to misdirect, frighten, and influence enemies.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Light Firearms","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Agility","Intelligence"],"bonusSkill":"Conjure Illusion","persona":["+5 Individual","+5 Criminal"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Signature Illusions","type":"Trait","text":"Choose a favored illusion type. Gain +2 to Illusion rolls with that type, and extend duration by +1 round for every ten character levels."},{"name":"Unnerved","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +1 to Wisdom or Perception saves against illusions for every five character levels."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/conjurer.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"14","description":"Illusionists often wander the streets on their lonesome. While they are tolerated more than the summoner, there is still significant disdain for summoners with many using their illusions to survive in the corporate zones that they travel. It is only a matter of when, not if an illusionist is caught by corporate law enforcement. This could be for something like trying to steal food to survive. Using illusions to have the security detail run into what appears a full team is usually enough for the illusionist to make their escape to survive another day."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2400000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Conjurers call spirits, illusions, phantasms, and other willing entities into reality.","disciplineSummary":"A caster who creates illusions and phantasms to misdirect, frighten, and influence enemies.","abilities":[{"name":"Signature Illusions","type":"Trait","text":"Choose a favored illusion type. Gain +2 to Illusion rolls with that type, and extend duration by +1 round for every ten character levels."},{"name":"Unnerved","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +1 to Wisdom or Perception saves against illusions for every five character levels."}],"profession":"Conjurer","discipline":"Illusionist"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"c00e6bfb345cfde4","name":"Tracker","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.infiltrator.tracker","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.infiltrator","profession":"Infiltrator","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":6600000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Infiltrator","discipline":"Tracker","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"c04be082b5c3959b","name":"Cyber Tech","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.software.cyber-tech","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.software","profession":"Software","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":4100000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Software","discipline":"Cyber Tech","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"c1336426f84a587d","name":"Acrobat","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/gymnast.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.gymnast.acrobat","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.gymnast","profession":"Gymnast","summary":"A nimble specialist in maneuverability and flexibility who moves through difficult spaces with ease.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Finesse","primaryAttributes":["Dexterity","Agility"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Agility"],"bonusSkill":"Escape","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Individual"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Trained Gymnast","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +3 to Athletics dice roll results."},{"name":"Improved Maneuverability","type":"Trait","text":"Difficult terrain, crates, rubble, and similar obstacles do not impede your movement."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/gymnast.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"4","description":"Acrobats are the lesser known Gymnast. This is due to their slippery nature of getting away even if they are captured. Formative years of many Acrobats have been spent in advanced gymnastics with many having cross trained across dance, swimming, vaulting, ice skating or other popular sports.\n\nAcrobats are untrained with specific weapons, however they tend to favor chakrams which can be thrown and return to the Acrobat with enough practice. Chakrams may have glyphs upon them for additional effects."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":400000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Gymnasts are flexible, dexterous, and agile specialists who move through cities, wilds, and difficult spaces with finesse.","disciplineSummary":"A nimble specialist in maneuverability and flexibility who moves through difficult spaces with ease.","abilities":[{"name":"Trained Gymnast","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +3 to Athletics dice roll results."},{"name":"Improved Maneuverability","type":"Trait","text":"Difficult terrain, crates, rubble, and similar obstacles do not impede your movement."}],"profession":"Gymnast","discipline":"Acrobat"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"c1c20f1aa0296ee1","name":"Geo Adept","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/elemental-adept.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.elemental-adept.geo-adept","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.elemental-adept","profession":"Elemental Adept","summary":"A geomancer who alters the ground for crowd control and defensive magic.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Geo Magic","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Strength"],"bonusAttributes":["Agility","Intelligence"],"bonusSkill":"Reading of Stone","persona":["+5 Individual","+5 Ruthless"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Geo Affinity","type":"Trait","text":"Geo spells gain +5 to attack rolls, +1 more every 10 levels, and +1d8 damage at level 5 and every 5 levels thereafter."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/elemental-adept.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"16","description":"Geo Adepts hail from the planet Kadion. With its vast mountainous ranges, steep ravines, and endless deserts Kadions quickly adapted to the terrain before their agricultural revolution. The first Geo Adepts used their abilities to carve out sections of the soil to make way for small buildings.\n\nAs geomancy became more known, the villages erupted into what is known as the Thousand Year War. Geomancy was used to slaughter entire villages as landslides were created. What remained of the four great houses of Kadion, each taking one of the major continents at the end of the war. With the treaty signed, each great house revered using Geomancy as a sacred art. Students must pass exams from all houses to be granted the rank of adept."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2700000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Elemental Adepts train in schools of elemental magic to alter reality through water, earth, fire, air, steel, or all elements.","disciplineSummary":"A geomancer who alters the ground for crowd control and defensive magic.","abilities":[{"name":"Geo Affinity","type":"Trait","text":"Geo spells gain +5 to attack rolls, +1 more every 10 levels, and +1d8 damage at level 5 and every 5 levels thereafter."}],"profession":"Elemental Adept","discipline":"Geo Adept"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"c4226dbd4d066161","name":"Con Artist","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.negotiator.con-artist","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.negotiator","profession":"Negotiator","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":6100000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Negotiator","discipline":"Con Artist","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"c43e2ce928c22ad3","name":"Chemist","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-1.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.field-technician.chemist","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.field-technician","profession":"Field Technician","summary":"A field crafter who can synthesize toxins and create dangerous chemical tools on the fly.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Combustibles","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Focus"],"bonusSkill":"Chemistry","persona":["+5 Ruthless","+5 Individual"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Improvised Toxin Grenade","type":"Action >>","text":"Create an Improved Toxin Grenade during an excursion and roll 1d10 for quality. Twice per Field Recovery."},{"name":"Mad Scientist","type":"Trait","text":"When crafting a chemical item, increase quality by 2 and produce a second item of the same quality without extra materials."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-1.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"8","description":"Often spending most of their time in a lab, Chemists work for long hours creating their perfect concoction. When drafted into a battlefield, they will find whatever components they need to synthesize toxins. Trained Chemists can clear an entire garrison with a single toxin grenade. When not on the battlefield, you may find a Chemist holed up in a vehicle creating something with a bit of an edge."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1100000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Field Technicians solve problems with chemistry, companions, explosives, and emergency medical work.","disciplineSummary":"A field crafter who can synthesize toxins and create dangerous chemical tools on the fly.","abilities":[{"name":"Improvised Toxin Grenade","type":"Action >>","text":"Create an Improved Toxin Grenade during an excursion and roll 1d10 for quality. Twice per Field Recovery."},{"name":"Mad Scientist","type":"Trait","text":"When crafting a chemical item, increase quality by 2 and produce a second item of the same quality without extra materials."}],"profession":"Field Technician","discipline":"Chemist"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"cade4440d1976264","name":"Paladin","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/vanguard.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.vanguard.paladin","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.vanguard","profession":"Vanguard","summary":"A defender using vitalism and divine magic to augment defense and restore allies.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Sword & Light Shield","primaryAttributes":["Strength","Reaction"],"bonusAttributes":["Reaction","Intelligence"],"bonusSkill":"Throw Shield","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Collectivist"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Reprisal","type":"Ability","text":"With a shield equipped, retaliate after blocking a melee attack. The strike uses the current round's multi-attack penalty and costs no action or reaction."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/vanguard.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"6","description":"Paladins are the stalwart protectors of the galaxy and belong to the Galactic Federation. Anyone interested in a Division that specializes in defending civilians can join the Paladins. Through brutal training frail individuals are reforged into reliable defenders. Paladins are quickly trained to use heals and shields. While magic can be used in a pinch, Paladins' strength comes from their versatility.\n\nThe GPD sends Paladins across the galaxy to handle smaller nuisances. Nuisances can be as simple as stepping in for a local conflict between settlements, restoring infrastructure, or more intensive nuisances such as evacuating citizens from Qeamite invasions.\n\nDedication between Paladins is near unbreakable. The bonds between Paladins last for life, being recognizable for many years after completing service to the GPD. A GPD veteran is still a force to be reckoned with."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":800000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Vanguards protect allies by drawing attacks and fire. They rely on physical shields, heavy armor, and energy shields.","disciplineSummary":"A defender using vitalism and divine magic to augment defense and restore allies.","abilities":[{"name":"Reprisal","type":"Ability","text":"With a shield equipped, retaliate after blocking a melee attack. The strike uses the current round's multi-attack penalty and costs no action or reaction."}],"profession":"Vanguard","discipline":"Paladin"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"d50674bb44f53104","name":"Summoner","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/conjurer.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.conjurer.summoner","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.conjurer","profession":"Conjurer","summary":"A spirit caller who summons beings for tasks, reconnaissance, and combat assistance.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Foci","primaryAttributes":["Wisdom","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Intelligence","Wisdom"],"bonusSkill":"Summon Eidolon","persona":["+5 Individual","+5 Criminal"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Established Connection","type":"Trait","text":"When summoning a spirit, gain +1 to the summoning roll for every five character levels."},{"name":"Innate Connection","type":"Trait","text":"Reduce the number of actions required to summon a spirit by one."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/conjurer.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"14","description":"Hunted by theological institutions, Summoners are always on the run. Their ability to summon entities from other dimensions have been declared heresy by a majority of theological institutions.\n\nThe Grand Church of Elatashi declared that all acts of summoning the dead unethical and heresy in 138 GE. After the declaration Summoners have been running from the pursuit of Holy Clerics sent by the Grand Church. Most Summoners operate on their own. Occasionally they will operate within a group that they can trust. That trust does not come easy from a Summoner as they place their life in the hands of allies."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2300000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Conjurers call spirits, illusions, phantasms, and other willing entities into reality.","disciplineSummary":"A spirit caller who summons beings for tasks, reconnaissance, and combat assistance.","abilities":[{"name":"Established Connection","type":"Trait","text":"When summoning a spirit, gain +1 to the summoning roll for every five character levels."},{"name":"Innate Connection","type":"Trait","text":"Reduce the number of actions required to summon a spirit by one."}],"profession":"Conjurer","discipline":"Summoner"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"d7a81feb7d0436d4","name":"Synergist","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/amplifier.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.amplifier.synergist","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.amplifier","profession":"Amplifier","summary":"A team-focused caster who enhances allies, debuffs enemies, and manipulates tempo.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Afflictions","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Focus","Wisdom"],"bonusSkill":"Haste","persona":["+5 Individual","+5 Ruthless"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Expanded Synergy","type":"Ability","text":"When casting a spell with the buff trait on an ally, also apply it to yourself or another ally at half mana cost rounded up. Three uses per Field Recovery."},{"name":"Efficient Afflictions","type":"Trait","text":"Spells with the debuff trait gain +1 effective level, without exceeding maximum spell level."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/amplifier.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"12","description":"Synergists often work in teams. Their abilities to enhance allies and inhibit their targets leaves every organization and group wanting a Synergist.\n\nA Synergist usually learns to tap into magic from a moment of extreme desperation. The fear that they experience lends to them being able to feel the strings of magic. Upon feeling the strings for the first time, reality around them appears to move at an affiau's pace. This fear that they have manifested has the Synergist become ruthless, either standing up for whatever personal cause they may have or for their own benefit. Since the onset of magic there have been increasing reports of law officials meeting their untimely demise."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1900000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Amplifiers enhance themselves and allies while inhibiting enemies with specialized intrinsic magic.","disciplineSummary":"A team-focused caster who enhances allies, debuffs enemies, and manipulates tempo.","abilities":[{"name":"Expanded Synergy","type":"Ability","text":"When casting a spell with the buff trait on an ally, also apply it to yourself or another ally at half mana cost rounded up. Three uses per Field Recovery."},{"name":"Efficient Afflictions","type":"Trait","text":"Spells with the debuff trait gain +1 effective level, without exceeding maximum spell level."}],"profession":"Amplifier","discipline":"Synergist"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"d8a8bb4ea8a1d413","name":"Fabricator","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.hardware.fabricator","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.hardware","profession":"Hardware","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":3900000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Hardware","discipline":"Fabricator","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"dd46d87873a9e087","name":"Stormtrooper","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/marksman-2.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.marksman.stormtrooper","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.marksman","profession":"Marksman","summary":"A trained soldier who keeps moving between cover while firing assault rifles.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Assault Rifles","primaryAttributes":["Dexterity","Reaction"],"bonusAttributes":["Strength","Reaction"],"bonusSkill":"Assault Rifles","persona":["+10 Collectivist"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Run & Gun","type":"Trait","text":"With an assault rifle equipped, making an attack roll while sprinting does not end your sprint."},{"name":"Momentum","type":"Trait","text":"When sprinting, roll 2d4 and add the result in meters rounded up to your sprint distance."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/marksman-2.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"11","description":"The Military is under the direct orders of the appointed Federation Commander. The Assault Corps is one of the branches of the Military Division. Stormtroopers in the Assault Corps are the first line of defense against incursions into Federation territory.\n\nDuring a Stormtrooper's tour of duty they often see species from uncharted regions. Per the Galactic Federation, Chisnoids should be avoided at any cost. Coming into contact with a Chisnoid, the order for retreat is immediately given. Countless numbers of Stormtroopers have been Uplifted and lost to the Chisnoid threat.\n\nA rare occurrence is coming across an extra-dimensional being. Any Stormtrooper who has come across one of these phantasms says that it is a death sentence. Creatures of fire, mana, shadow, and dreams haunt the Stormtroopers that have encountered them."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1700000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Marksmen leave their mark with projectile weapons and often specialize in a favored style of firearm or bow.","disciplineSummary":"A trained soldier who keeps moving between cover while firing assault rifles.","abilities":[{"name":"Run & Gun","type":"Trait","text":"With an assault rifle equipped, making an attack roll while sprinting does not end your sprint."},{"name":"Momentum","type":"Trait","text":"When sprinting, roll 2d4 and add the result in meters rounded up to your sprint distance."}],"profession":"Marksman","discipline":"Stormtrooper"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"e44353582faed782","name":"Auto-Mechanic","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.mechanic.auto-mechanic","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.mechanic","profession":"Mechanic","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":4500000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Mechanic","discipline":"Auto-Mechanic","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"e60c447427b339ea","name":"Marine Operator","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.vehicle-pilot.marine-operator","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.vehicle-pilot","profession":"Vehicle Pilot","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":4900000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Vehicle Pilot","discipline":"Marine Operator","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"e899c108726ae3c9","name":"Fist Fighter","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/martial-artist.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.martial-artist.fist-fighter","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.martial-artist","profession":"Martial Artist","summary":"A slow, heavy-hitting martial combatant who grapples, throws, trips, and pins foes.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Melee","primaryAttributes":["Strength","Reaction"],"bonusAttributes":["Strength","Reaction"],"bonusSkill":"Grapple","persona":["+5 Ruthless","+5 Individual"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Second Wind","type":"Reaction","text":"When lethal damage would knock you out, prevent the lethal result and set your HP to 1 after the attack resolves. Once per long rest."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/martial-artist.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"5","description":"The Fist Fighter uses a form of martial arts styles that started as Bar-fighting, Boxing, Karate, Jujitsu and Sumo Wrestling in 20th century Terra Prime and evolved into its own martial art called Gio Feign. Gio Feign training has the Fist Fighter learning to endure being hit despite the exhaustive nature of the Martial Art allowing them to get a second wind. Staples of Gio Feign include grappling, throwing, tripping or intimidating their opponent. Gio Feign is popular among the Planetary Union with training facilities dotting the cityscapes throughout the galaxy.\n\nFist Fighter gets up close and personal using the tactics of Gio Feign to manipulate the moment using their target's strength against them and pin them down. Their advantage often leaves their opponent beaten and humiliated in a crowd."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":600000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Martial Artists refine body, discipline, and precision through combat traditions passed down across generations.","disciplineSummary":"A slow, heavy-hitting martial combatant who grapples, throws, trips, and pins foes.","abilities":[{"name":"Second Wind","type":"Reaction","text":"When lethal damage would knock you out, prevent the lethal result and set your HP to 1 after the attack resolves. Once per long rest."}],"profession":"Martial Artist","discipline":"Fist Fighter"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"ee69208c7834ee30","name":"Shapeshifter","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/druid.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.druid.shapeshifter","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.druid","profession":"Druid","summary":"A fauna-form specialist who attacks, intimidates, communicates, and navigates as animals.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Animal Forms","primaryAttributes":["Wisdom","Strength"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Wisdom"],"bonusSkill":"Fauna Speak","persona":["+5 Individual","+5 Criminal"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Commune with Fauna","type":"Trait","text":"Communicate with fauna as if speaking your native language, limited by your current form."},{"name":"Hastened Shapeshifting","type":"Trait","text":"When shifting into animal form, roll 1d6 and reduce the action point cost by the result."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/druid.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"15","description":"Druids that shapeshift are generally known as Shapeshifters to the rest of the galaxy. Their ability to shift their form comes natural to them. They have been known to take the forms of smaller critters to even portraying something as large as a greater dragon.\n\nShapeshifters take fauna forms to communicate with other fauna gleaning information that otherwise may not have been noticed. They also use their fauna forms to increase their senses preparing for danger, before danger can come to the enclave. A shapeshifter will lay down their life for their community. Fear bleeds into the eyes of those that dare to attack."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2500000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Druids commune with nature and stabilize Aether disrupted by corporations and reckless magic users.","disciplineSummary":"A fauna-form specialist who attacks, intimidates, communicates, and navigates as animals.","abilities":[{"name":"Commune with Fauna","type":"Trait","text":"Communicate with fauna as if speaking your native language, limited by your current form."},{"name":"Hastened Shapeshifting","type":"Trait","text":"When shifting into animal form, roll 1d6 and reduce the action point cost by the result."}],"profession":"Druid","discipline":"Shapeshifter"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"f026404fdf4c4d29","name":"Aerial Operator","type":"discipline","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.vehicle-pilot.aerial-operator","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.vehicle-pilot","profession":"Vehicle Pilot","summary":"","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"","primaryAttributes":[],"bonusAttributes":[],"bonusSkill":"","persona":[],"tags":[],"abilities":[],"pageImage":"","source":"","sourcePage":"","description":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":5000000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"profession":"Vehicle Pilot","discipline":"Aerial Operator","abilities":[]}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"f21d5446a3491a35","name":"Priest","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/cleric.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.cleric.priest","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.cleric","profession":"Cleric","summary":"A holy support caster focused on healing allies and damaging undead with vitality.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Staff","primaryAttributes":["Wisdom","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Intelligence","Wisdom"],"bonusSkill":"Healing Touch","persona":["+5 Collectivist","+5 Empathetic"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Pray","type":"Sustained Action >>","text":"Chant in prayer, consuming 10 stamina each combat round. Heal creatures within 10m for 2d8 + Wisdom HP at the end of your turn; undead instead take vitality damage with a Wisdom save."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/cleric.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"13","description":"Priests are often respected members of clergy to their religions. When not preoccupied with their holy duties, a Priest can often be found within their community healing the sick and wounded. These individuals are often considered paragons within their communities, housing the unfortunate, and caring for those in need."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2100000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Clerics are devout religious advocates who heal, defend, spread faith, and sometimes enforce doctrine.","disciplineSummary":"A holy support caster focused on healing allies and damaging undead with vitality.","abilities":[{"name":"Pray","type":"Sustained Action >>","text":"Chant in prayer, consuming 10 stamina each combat round. Heal creatures within 10m for 2d8 + Wisdom HP at the end of your turn; undead instead take vitality damage with a Wisdom save."}],"profession":"Cleric","discipline":"Priest"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"f60bce432eeb5821","name":"Demolitionist","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-2.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.field-technician.demolitionist","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.field-technician","profession":"Field Technician","summary":"An explosive specialist who disarms bombs and turns structural weaknesses into bigger blasts.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Light Firearms","primaryAttributes":["Intelligence","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Dexterity","Focus"],"bonusSkill":"Explosives","persona":["+5 Ruthless","+5 Individual"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Knack for Disarming","type":"Trait","text":"Add Explosives skill level to disarming rolls against explosives."},{"name":"Sense Structural Weakness","type":"Trait","text":"When placing explosives on artillery, drones, or vehicles with the mechanical trait, add 1d4 explosive damage per Explosives level."},{"name":"Explosives go Boom!","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +2d6 damage with explosives, and add Explosives level to attack rolls using explosive weapons or ammunition."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-2.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"9","description":"Demolitionists are explosive experts. Watching things go boom is a favorite pastime of Demolitionists. In the distance you can hear the explosions of nitroglycerin with foliage bursting various directions. While in the field Demolitionists are treated with caution as it is unknown when you will hear explosions."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1300000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Field Technicians solve problems with chemistry, companions, explosives, and emergency medical work.","disciplineSummary":"An explosive specialist who disarms bombs and turns structural weaknesses into bigger blasts.","abilities":[{"name":"Knack for Disarming","type":"Trait","text":"Add Explosives skill level to disarming rolls against explosives."},{"name":"Sense Structural Weakness","type":"Trait","text":"When placing explosives on artillery, drones, or vehicles with the mechanical trait, add 1d4 explosive damage per Explosives level."},{"name":"Explosives go Boom!","type":"Trait","text":"Gain +2d6 damage with explosives, and add Explosives level to attack rolls using explosive weapons or ammunition."}],"profession":"Field Technician","discipline":"Demolitionist"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"f8fcc2553982f6c3","name":"Beast Tamer","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-1.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.field-technician.beast-tamer","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.field-technician","profession":"Field Technician","summary":"A creature handler who can pacify hostile beasts and benefit from a companion's senses.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Light Firearms","primaryAttributes":["Dexterity","Focus"],"bonusAttributes":["Charisma","Perception"],"bonusSkill":"Train Creature","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Lawful"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Overriding Dominance","type":"Action >>","text":"Roll Train Creature + Charisma against a hostile creature. Outcomes range from no effect to pacified, allied, or tamed for the encounter."},{"name":"Enhanced Senses","type":"Trait","text":"With a creature companion summoned, you may use the companion's Perception modifier for tracking, detection, or perception rolls."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/field-technician-1.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"8","description":"Beast Tamers are known for being able to confront wild creatures that attack them, either pacifying them or having the creature turn on its allies. Tamers are usually on less developed worlds finding their next companion."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1200000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Field Technicians solve problems with chemistry, companions, explosives, and emergency medical work.","disciplineSummary":"A creature handler who can pacify hostile beasts and benefit from a companion's senses.","abilities":[{"name":"Overriding Dominance","type":"Action >>","text":"Roll Train Creature + Charisma against a hostile creature. Outcomes range from no effect to pacified, allied, or tamed for the encounter."},{"name":"Enhanced Senses","type":"Trait","text":"With a creature companion summoned, you may use the companion's Perception modifier for tracking, detection, or perception rolls."}],"profession":"Field Technician","discipline":"Beast Tamer"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"f98762a9c28c2726","name":"Adjudicator","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/cleric.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.cleric.adjudicator","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.cleric","profession":"Cleric","summary":"An offensive church warrior who fights at the front with a great hammer and divine protection.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Great Hammer","primaryAttributes":["Strength","Intelligence"],"bonusAttributes":["Strength","Wisdom"],"bonusSkill":"Divine Bolt","persona":["+5 Ruthless","+5 Collectivist"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Divine Veil","type":"Ability","text":"Become immune to non-lethal physical damage for 1d4 rounds. After it fades, roll 2d10 days before your deity answers again."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/cleric.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"13","description":"Adjudicators are feared warriors of the churches that they represent. When a religious crusade is declared, Adjudicators are the harbingers of destruction in their deity's name. If the population does not convert to the church's religion, Adjudicators suppress or decimate anyone who does not submit.\n\nThe Galactic Federation allows adjudicators to carry out their duties under the proclamation of religious freedom. This has resulted in multiple planetary systems operating under a theological monarchy. As long as resources and credits are sent to the Galactic Federation, theological dynasties are free to operate as they will.\n\nThe Galactic Federation does its best to maintain peace with theological planetary systems as to not become strained into a holy war with Adjudicators. The Galactic Federation keeps the status quo for the time being."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":2200000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Clerics are devout religious advocates who heal, defend, spread faith, and sometimes enforce doctrine.","disciplineSummary":"An offensive church warrior who fights at the front with a great hammer and divine protection.","abilities":[{"name":"Divine Veil","type":"Ability","text":"Become immune to non-lethal physical damage for 1d4 rounds. After it fades, roll 2d10 days before your deity answers again."}],"profession":"Cleric","discipline":"Adjudicator"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"fcb42605a43de742","name":"Ranger","type":"discipline","img":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/marksman-1.png","system":{"definitionId":"veilrunner.discipline.marksman.ranger","intents":["chargen-selectable"],"providedActionIds":[],"professionId":"veilrunner.profession.marksman","profession":"Marksman","summary":"A versatile medium-range attacker whose flexibility comes from specialized arrows.","quote":"","primaryWeapon":"Bow","primaryAttributes":["Dexterity","Agility"],"bonusAttributes":["Charisma","Dexterity"],"bonusSkill":"Bows","persona":["+5 Empathetic","+5 Criminal"],"tags":[],"abilities":[{"name":"Successive Arrows","type":"Action >>","text":"With a bow equipped, fire three declared arrows. Attacks count toward attack penalty, but the penalty applies after the action completes. Three uses per Field Recovery."}],"pageImage":"systems/veilrunner/assets/img/professions/marksman-1.png","source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","sourcePage":"10","description":"Prior to becoming a Ranger, many individuals have tried to get their five minutes of fame on the Galactic Video Feed. It is unknown what drives these individuals to become Rangers, but there is an uncanny correlation between influencers who become Rangers. The Galactic Federation tolerates these unruly individuals due to the combined successive effort of the Ranger's Guild to combat ecological terror. Rangers have helped maintain ecological order within national parks throughout the centuries.\n\nDuring their free time they are often found in taverns having a good time boasting stories of wild adventures they have been on, that is if they are to be believed. One common legend states that a lone ranger successfully captivated a dragon on charisma alone before taking its hoard of treasures. The Galactic Federation does not condone such acts and exercises the right to exile any individual that partakes in such act."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":1600000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"veilrunner":{"source":"Veilrunner 2026.07.30.pdf","professionSummary":"Marksmen leave their mark with projectile weapons and often specialize in a favored style of firearm or bow.","disciplineSummary":"A versatile medium-range attacker whose flexibility comes from specialized arrows.","abilities":[{"name":"Successive Arrows","type":"Action >>","text":"With a bow equipped, fire three declared arrows. Attacks count toward attack penalty, but the penalty applies after the action completes. Three uses per Field Recovery."}],"profession":"Marksman","discipline":"Ranger"}},"_stats":{"systemId":"Veilrunner","systemVersion":"0.0.16","coreVersion":"14.365","createdTime":1787443200000,"modifiedTime":1787443200000,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
